# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vercel mirror of the Firebase site.
#
# The published site is the committed output at this directory's root: HTML,
# sitemap.xml / sitemap.txt / sitemap-index.xml, rss.xml, robots.txt, assets/.
# Everything below is build tooling or backend source that Firebase never serves
# anyway (firebase.json only serves files found on disk), so shipping it to
# Vercel would upload ~4 MB of dead weight and expose source paths.
#
# Syntax is gitignore-style, relative to the project root (this directory).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Build + QA tooling (Node/Python). Never part of the served site.
tools/
scripts/
node_modules/

# Backend source: Firebase Functions + Supabase Edge Functions, SQL, config.
functions/
supabase/

# Repository housekeeping and CI. Vercel has no use for either.
.github/
.claude/
.firebaserc
firebase.json
package.json
package-lock.json
.gitignore
.vercelignore

# Internal notes / audit reports. Not linked from any page, not in the sitemap,
# and several contain operational detail that should not be publicly fetchable.
*.md

# Local editor + OS debris.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# Secret-bearing files (already gitignored, listed again as a belt-and-braces
# guard in case a local run leaves one behind in the upload).
.env
.env.*
gsc-*.json
service-account*.json
*credentials*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored, because the whole point of this deployment is to
# test whether Google can fetch them from a Vercel host:
#   sitemap.xml  google-sitemap.xml  sitemap-index.xml  sitemap.txt
#   rss.xml  robots.txt  ads.txt  llms.txt  llms-full.txt
#   manifest.webmanifest  sw.js  404.html  index.html  assets/**
#   .well-known/security.txt  and every committed *.html page
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
